{"id":"3b4ba78a-f7ba-492f-b072-2b789cf2a061","object":"chat.completion","created":1785001155,"model":"deepseek-v4-flash","choices":[{"index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","content":"{\"implementation\":\"def solve(case):\\n    threshold = case['threshold']\\n    calls = case['calls']\\n    accepted_call_ids = []\\n    diagnostics = []\\n    for call in calls:\\n        call_id = call['call_id']\\n        loss_without = call['loss_without_call']\\n        loss_with = call['loss_with_call']\\n        tokens = call['prediction_tokens']\\n        if not isinstance(tokens, (int, float)) or tokens <= 0:\\n            raise ValueError(\\\"prediction_tokens must be a positive number\\\")\\n        parseable = call['parseable']\\n        gain = loss_without - loss_with\\n        normalized_gain = gain / tokens\\n        accepted = bool(parseable and normalized_gain >= threshold)\\n        if accepted:\\n            accepted_call_ids.append(call_id)\\n        diagnostics.append({\\n            \\\"call_id\\\": call_id,\\n            \\\"accepted\\\": accepted,\\n            \\\"normalized_gain\\\": round(normalized_gain, 6)\\n        })\\n    return {\\n        \\\"accepted_call_ids\\\": accepted_call_ids,\\n        \\\"diagnostics\\\": diagnostics\\n    }\"}","reasoning_content":"We need to implement solve(case) based on the description. The task is \"AGENT-TF-01\". The payload has \"threshold\" and \"calls\" array. Each call has call_id, loss_without_call, loss_with_call, prediction_tokens, parseable.\n\nWe compute gain = loss_without_call - loss_with_call. Then normalized_gain = gain / prediction_tokens. Then accept if parseable is true and normalized_gain >= threshold. Also we need to output diagnostics ordered by call order (as in input). accepted_call_ids is list of accepted call_ids in order.\n\nOutput: {\"accepted_call_ids\": [...], \"diagnostics\": [{\"call_id\": ..., \"accepted\": bool, \"normalized_gain\": float}]}. The normalized_gain should be rounded? The description says \"rounded per-call diagnostics\". The output schema allows number type, but we should round? Possibly to some precision? The fixture examples don't show expected output. But we need to follow the description: \"Return accepted call IDs and rounded per-call diagnostics.\" And the output schema says \"type\": \"number\" for normalized_gain. We should round to, say, 6 decimal places? Since inputs are floats with many decimals, common rounding might be to a certain decimal. However, the instructions say \"rounded\" but not specify precision. We could compute and use round(x, 6) or maybe round to some standard like 8? But to be safe, I'll use round to 6 decimal places as typical. However, the problem might expect exact floating point values without rounding? The phrase \"rounded per-call diagnostics\" suggests we should round. In past similar tasks, they used round to 6 decimal places. I'll assume that.\n\nAlso note: The function must not mutate case. We'll copy or just read.\n\nImplementation: For each call in case['calls'], compute gain, normalized_gain, check parseable and normalized_gain >= threshold (inclusive threshold). Build accepted_call_ids and diagnostics.\n\nAlso we should validate that threshold is present, calls is list, each call has required fields. If missing, raise ValueError.\n\nWe must output exactly the structure as per schema.\n\nEdge cases: If no calls, empty arrays.\n\nNow, produce Python source code for solve(case). Must be in JSON string.\n\nWe'll write:\n\ndef solve(case):\n    threshold = case['threshold']\n    calls = case['calls']\n    accepted = []\n    diagnostics = []\n    for call in calls:\n        call_id = call['call_id']\n        loss_without = call['loss_without_call']\n        loss_with = call['loss_with_call']\n        tokens = call['prediction_tokens']\n        parseable = call['parseable']\n        if not isinstance(tokens, (int, float)) or tokens <= 0:\n            raise ValueError(\"prediction_tokens must be positive\")\n        gain = loss_without - loss_with\n        normalized_gain = gain / tokens\n        accepted_flag = parseable and normalized_gain >= threshold\n        if accepted_flag:\n            accepted.append(call_id)\n        diagnostics.append({\n            \"call_id\": call_id,\n            \"accepted\": accepted_flag,\n            \"normalized_gain\": round(normalized_gain, 6)\n        })\n    return {\n        \"accepted_call_ids\": accepted,\n        \"diagnostics\": diagnostics\n    }\n\nBut careful: The threshold is inclusive \"at or above threshold\". So >=.\n\nAlso note: The description mentions \"Use only quantities present in the case payload.\" So all good.\n\nWe must ensure the function returns the exact JSON-serializable dict.\n\nNow we need to wrap in JSON: {\"implementation\": \"def solve(case):\\n ...\"} with proper escaping.\n\nWe'll produce the implementation string.\n\nLet's write the full response."},"logprobs":null,"finish_reason":"stop"}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":2171,"completion_tokens":1060,"total_tokens":3231,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":2048},"completion_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":794},"prompt_cache_hit_tokens":2048,"prompt_cache_miss_tokens":123},"system_fingerprint":"fp_8b330d02d0_prod0820_fp8_kvcache_20260402"}